From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Subject: [PATCH] _mingw.h: spell the aarch64 __fastfail inline __inline__

woarm64-0001 defines __MINGW_FASTFAIL_INLINE as "static inline" for
aarch64.  "inline" is not a keyword in C89/C90, so every -std=c89 (or
-ansi) translation unit that includes <windows.h> fails to compile
("expected ';' before 'void'"); serf builds with -std=c89.  The GNU
spelling works in every C mode, like the __MINGW_INTRIN_INLINE used on
the other targets.

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
---
--- a/mingw-w64-headers/crt/_mingw.h.in
+++ b/mingw-w64-headers/crt/_mingw.h.in
@@ -625,7 +625,7 @@
 #if defined(__aarch64__)
 /* Inline fails for aarch64 */
 #define __MINGW_FASTFAIL_INLINE_DECL static
-#define __MINGW_FASTFAIL_INLINE static inline
+#define __MINGW_FASTFAIL_INLINE static __inline__
 #else
 #define __MINGW_FASTFAIL_INLINE_DECL
 #define __MINGW_FASTFAIL_INLINE __MINGW_INTRIN_INLINE
